{"name":"Bashful Emu","hex":"#b2b0ac","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bashful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Shy; not liking to be noticed; socially timid.","Indicating bashfulness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bashful"},{"term":"emu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Eastern Muria."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large flightless bird native to Australia, Dromaius novaehollandiae. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A cassowary (genus Casuarius)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emu","blocks":[{"text":"The emu is a species of flightless bird endemic to Australia, where it is the tallest native bird. It is the only extant member of the genus Dromaius and the third-tallest living bird after its African ratite relatives, the common ostrich and Somali ostrich. The emu's native ranges cover most of the Australian mainland. The Tasmanian, Kangaroo Island and King Island subspecies became extinct after the European settlement of Australia in 1788."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Emu_1_-_Tidbinbilla.jpg/330px-Emu_1_-_Tidbinbilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emu","wikidata":"Q93208"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Emu_skeleton.jpg/500px-Emu_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Emu_skeleton.jpg/500px-Emu_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mounted skeleton","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmu_skeleton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jpg/500px-Dromaius_novaehollandiae_-zoo_-two_feet.jp